// @check
// @error '__add_f32x4__' is a compiler intrinsic and cannot be redefined
// The SIMD intrinsics are dispatched by CALLEE NAME before any declaration lookup, so a user
// function of the same name would be silently discarded (the same hazard the memory intrinsics
// guard against). The rule is the name, at the definition — see intrinsics/error-redefine-intrinsic.vl.
function __add_f32x4__(a: i32, b: i32) { return a + b }
print(__add_f32x4__(1, 2))
